        "text": "No - $50/month per broker connection covers unlimited Bulenox accounts. Compared to other automation tools that charge $25-$50 per account per month, PMT's pricing model is built for traders running multiple Bulenox Master Accounts in parallel."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What platforms does Bulenox support?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bulenox is a Rithmic-based firm. Primary supported platforms are Rithmic R|Trader Pro and NinjaTrader 8. Additional supported platforms include Tiger Trade, Quantower, and ATAS. Sierra Chart, MotiveWave, and Bookmap also work via Rithmic. TradingView is supported for charting and alerts via webhook bridges like PickMyTrade - it is not a direct execution platform. Tradovate is NOT a direct Bulenox platform."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Rithmic the default Bulenox platform?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - Rithmic is the default and primary Bulenox platform. All Bulenox accounts route through the Rithmic system. Rithmic suits traders using NinjaTrader 8, Sierra Chart, R|Trader Pro, Quantower, ATAS, or Bookmap. There is no native Tradovate option on Bulenox."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I switch front-end platforms (Rithmic, NinjaTrader, Quantower) after signup?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - because all front-ends route to the same Rithmic system, you can switch between Rithmic R|Trader Pro, NinjaTrader 8, Tiger Trade, Quantower, ATAS, Sierra Chart, and Bookmap without changing accounts. There is no Tradovate option to switch to or from - Bulenox does not support Tradovate directly."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I connect TradingView to Bulenox?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TradingView has no native Bulenox integration. You bridge it through PickMyTrade: TradingView alert - PMT webhook - PMT routes the order to your Bulenox account via Rithmic. Setup takes about 10 minutes once your PMT and Bulenox accounts are linked."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Bulenox use ProjectX?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. As of February 2026, ProjectX is exclusive to Topstep - other firms like MFFU, TickTick Trader, Tradeify and Bulenox do not use ProjectX. Bulenox runs natively on Rithmic. Verify on bulenox.com if you need the latest, but ProjectX has not been an option for Bulenox traders."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are there platform fees on top of the evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Rithmic R|Trader Pro is free to use with Bulenox. CME Pro live data is approximately $30/month for non-pro feed users (free for retail non-pro). NinjaTrader 8 free version covers Bulenox basics; live data fees apply. Quantower, ATAS, and Tiger Trade each have their own license fees on top - verify per-platform pricing on each vendor's site."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does NinjaTrader work with Bulenox?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - NinjaTrader 8 connects to Bulenox via Rithmic. NinjaScript bots run natively. NinjaTrader's Strategy Analyzer, Market Analyzer, and Order Flow indicators all work on Bulenox sim accounts. Free NT8 plus Rithmic is the most common setup for chart-heavy Bulenox traders."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use Sierra Chart or Quantower?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - both connect to Bulenox via Rithmic. Sierra Chart and Quantower are popular among professional Bulenox traders for their depth-of-market and spread tools. PickMyTrade integrates with both via the underlying Rithmic system."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is mobile trading supported?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes via Tiger Trade mobile and TradingView Mobile (iOS/Android), and via the Rithmic mobile front-end. NinjaTrader Mobile is limited and not recommended. PickMyTrade users running TradingView mobile alerts can route trades from anywhere with cell service - fully hands-free Bulenox trading."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which platform should a beginner pick?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tiger Trade or Quantower for the easiest learning curve, both connected via Rithmic. Once you want richer charting and bots, move to NinjaTrader 8 (free). All routes ultimately go through Rithmic, so you can swap front-ends without changing your Bulenox account. TradingView pairs cleanly with PickMyTrade as the webhook bridge into Rithmic."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I reset a failed Bulenox evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Bulenox offers a paid reset that re-zeros the evaluation balance and re-activates the trailing drawdown buffer without requiring a new full purchase. Reset is cheaper than a fresh purchase at full price but more expensive than a fresh promo-coded purchase."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does a reset cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Approximately $80-$00 depending on account size - verify the current sliding scale at the Bulenox dashboard. The reset price is independent of original promo discounts; it's a one-time fee per reset."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are there reset discount codes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bulenox occasionally runs reset-specific promos (50% off resets, free reset weekends). Watch the Discord and the affiliate-network deal pages. End-of-month is the most common reset-promo window."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I get a refund on a failed evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Once you've placed at least one trade, the evaluation fee is non-refundable. This is industry standard. Pre-trade refund requests within a short window after purchase may be honored on a discretionary basis - open a support ticket immediately if you change your mind before placing a trade."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What about a refund on the activation fee?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Master Account activation fee (tiered: ~$98 on $0K up to ~$490 on $250K) is non-refundable. If your funded account breaches before you take a payout, the activation fee is gone. This is a sunk cost to budget for when planning Bulenox unit economics."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is reset cheaper than buying a new evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Usually yes vs. full-price new purchase, but often NO vs. a promo-coded fresh purchase. Run the math: a new $50K under an 80% off recurring promo can be cheaper than the $80-$00 reset fee. Check the active promo before resetting."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is there a limit to how many resets I can do?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No published limit. Some traders reset 3-5 times before passing. Bulenox doesn't blacklist serial-resetters as long as the account is paid for each cycle. Note: the Master Account itself cannot be reset - only the evaluation. A breached Master Account requires a fresh evaluation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Bulenox offer free resets via affiliate?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Some Bulenox affiliates run free-reset giveaways monthly. Watch prop firm forums contests and Discord giveaway threads. PickMyTrade does not offer Bulenox-reset codes directly but PMT users running multi-firm setups often qualify for community-affiliate reset bundles."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Bulenox have an affiliate program?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. The Bulenox affiliate program pays 10-15% recurring commission on referred evaluation purchases. Top affiliates report monthly commission income in the four-figure range. Apply via the Bulenox dashboard \"Affiliate\" tab."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Where do I find current Bulenox promo codes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Three sources: Bulenox's own Discord (most up-to-date), prop firm forums \"deals\" megathread (community-curated), and major prop-firm affiliate review sites. Codes typically rotate at the start of each calendar month."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are recurring discount codes really worth it vs. one-time?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes if you expect a 2+ month evaluation. A recurring 80% off code locks the discounted rate for the entire evaluation life - for a 3-month evaluation, that's 3x the savings of a first-month-only code. Choose recurring whenever it's available."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does PickMyTrade offer Bulenox bundle deals?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PickMyTrade does not bundle Bulenox evaluations directly, but PMT does run periodic \"first month free\" promotions on the $50/month PMT subscription that pair well with Bulenox discount months. Watch the PMT homepage and Discord for the current PMT-side offer."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I become a Bulenox-affiliated educator?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bulenox runs an \"ambassador\" program for content creators with proven payout history and an audience. Tier benefits include higher affiliate commission, custom codes, and co-marketing opportunities. Apply through the affiliate portal once you have a documented payout track record."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Bulenox vs Apex Trader Funding - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Apex is the largest US futures prop with the deepest scaling plan. Bulenox wins on EOD trailing (both Bulenox options trail on settled EOD balance versus Apex's intraday trailing) and on the 100% / first-$0K-then-90/10 split structure. Both firms require around $,000 for the first payout. Apex wins on brand maturity. Many traders run both side-by-side via PickMyTrade."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Bulenox vs Topstep - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Topstep is the OG futures prop (founded 2012) and runs on TopstepX (Topstep's ProjectX-based front-end - ProjectX is exclusive to Topstep as of February 2026). Bulenox runs on Rithmic with multiple front-ends (R|Trader Pro, NinjaTrader 8, Quantower, Tiger Trade, ATAS). Topstep's split scales; Bulenox is 100% on the first $0,000 of lifetime Master profits, then 90/10. Bulenox is more bot-friendly; Topstep is more brand-trusted."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Bulenox vs MyFundedFutures (MFFU)",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MFFU runs on its own front-end backed by Rithmic/Tradovate after being forced off ProjectX (ProjectX became Topstep-exclusive in early 2026). Bulenox is purely Rithmic-based. MFFU's plans include Core/Rapid/Pro/Builder/Flex tiers with aggressive 90%/100% splits; Bulenox offers 100% on the first $0K of lifetime Master profits then 90/10. MFFU's \"Eval\" model has tighter consistency rules; Bulenox uses a 40% best-day rule. Most multi-firm traders run both side-by-side via PickMyTrade."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Bulenox vs Tradeify",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tradeify was forced off ProjectX in early 2026 (ProjectX is now Topstep-exclusive) and has migrated to its own Rithmic-backed setup. Tradeify offers Advanced / Straight-to-Funded plans; Bulenox is more conservative in plan structure. Tradeify's payout cadence is similar to Bulenox's weekly Wednesday schedule; both pay roughly 90% with first-bracket bonuses. Bulenox supports a broader range of front-ends (NinjaTrader 8, Quantower, Tiger Trade, ATAS) via Rithmic."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Bulenox vs TickTick Trader (TPT)",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TickTick Trader was forced off ProjectX in early 2026 (Topstep is now the only firm on ProjectX) and has moved to a Rithmic-backed setup. TPT historically used a flat-fee approach and has lifetime-funded structures Bulenox doesn't match. Bulenox uses EOD trailing on both Option 1 and Option 2. Splits are roughly comparable. TPT is better for traders who want one-time fees; Bulenox is better for recurring-promo discount stackers."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Bulenox vs Earn2Trade",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Earn2Trade uses a more education-focused 2-step model with an LMS and instructor support. Bulenox is pure trading - no curriculum. E2T's profit splits scale 50% to 80%; Bulenox pays 100% on the first $0,000 of lifetime Master profits then 90/10. E2T for new traders who want education; Bulenox for experienced traders who want max payout efficiency."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why run Bulenox alongside other prop firms?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Diversification of firm-specific risk: rule changes, payout delays, platform migrations, sudden TOS amendments. Running Bulenox + Apex + MFFU + Tradeify simultaneously through PickMyTrade means a single bad firm-week doesn't kill your overall income. PMT's $50/month per broker connection makes this multi-firm strategy economical."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which firm pays out fastest?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bulenox typical processing is 1-3 business days, Apex similar, Topstep 2-5 days, MFFU 1-3 days. prop firm forums payout-tracker threads update monthly - Bulenox sits in the upper half of the speed ranking consistently. Crypto payouts (Wise/USDT) tend to clear fastest across all firms."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which firm is most automation-friendly?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bulenox is among the top tier alongside Tradeify and Earn2Trade. No HFT, no latency arb, but standard automation (TradingView, NinjaScript, EAs, Pine Script bots) is permitted without pre-approval. Apex is automation-friendly but has tighter trailing; Topstep restricts certain multi-account automation patterns."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I start with Bulenox or Apex?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If you're new to futures props, Bulenox's EOD trailing (on both Option 1 and Option 2) and the 100% / first-$0K-then-90/10 split make it forgiving on intraday MFE swings. If you want the deepest scaling and largest brand presence, Apex. Minimum payouts are similar (~$,000) at both. The optimal answer for most active traders is \"both\" - run them in parallel via PickMyTrade."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I set trading time restrictions in PickMyTrade for my Bulenox account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PickMyTrade includes a Trading Time feature available across all supported broker connections. You can configure specific active trading windows with start and end times (24-hour ET format). Any TradingView alerts received outside your configured hours are automatically rejected — no new trades are placed. Existing open positions remain active. Settings can be applied to specific accounts or all accounts at once. Full guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/trading-time-settings/"
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
